Hi Everyone,

I am currently working on IGS-5309. Implementing the exact scenario mentioned in the Jira ticket is challenging because the documents are fetched from **dpw-docstore**. Verifying the document availability of all requests simultaneously on the home screen would be complex and could also have a significant impact on application performance.

To address this, I have identified an alternative solution, and I am attaching a screenshot to the Jira ticket for your review.

In the proposed approach:
- A **Document (eye) icon** will be displayed in the Attachments column.
- When a user clicks the icon, the system will check whether documents are available for that specific request.
- If documents are available, they will be displayed to the user. If no documents are available, no documents will be shown.
- When the user clicks on an available document, they will be redirected to the Document Management screen, as required by the scenario.

This approach will help improve performance by processing one request at a time instead of checking document availability for all requests simultaneously. It will also reduce service dependencies and minimize the chances of failures.

I have attached the screenshot to the Jira ticket. Please review the proposed approach and share your feedback.

